+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Logs containing request/view events require a runtime that understands logged visibility."
+---
+# Logs with activity request views
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+A required `request/view` event records which existing messages remain visible. Older runtimes reject such logs instead of silently exposing hidden history. Existing logs without the event retain their behavior.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Back up session directories and install the matching Session, Token Meter and plugin packages together.
+2. Confirm both `ctx.sessions.requestViewVersion` and `ctx.tokenMeter.requestViewVersion` are `1` before enabling activity views. Context-breakdown and pressure checkpoints now use state version 6 and are refolded; billing totals retain their meaning.
+3. Keep the patched runtime when opening, replaying or exporting view-bearing logs. To roll back the application, restore the complete pre-deployment backup; never delete view records or mark them ignorable.
